    "sourceNotes": "The official programme is a three-year, 180-EC bachelor combining biology, chemistry, mathematics and process engineering. Years 1 and 2 each account for 60 EC in cell biology, microbiology, biochemistry, chemistry, mathematics, cell-factory and bioreactor design, process engineering, genetics, statistics, protein biochemistry, gene technology and separation-process design. The programme describes Biology and Engineering directions; Biology is selected by the neutral official-order tie-break because it is listed first, while published restricted choices remain generic. Year 3 contains a 24-EC laboratory thesis, 6 EC restricted choice and 30 EC genuine free choice/minor space.",
