  "selection": {
    "stoppingReason": "maximum-reached",
    "assessment": "The closest programme combines UCR’s strongest molecular, cellular, laboratory and quantitative foundations. Medical biotechnology and engineering/data directions are independently evidenced, coherent and mechanically feasible, and clear the pairwise distinctness floor. Sustainable biobased biotechnology remains evidenced but is not attempted after the three-alternative maximum."
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "different-curricular-structure",
      "placement": "comparison",
      "text": "WUR Biotechnology contains dedicated organic and analytical chemistry, thermodynamics, cell-factory and bioreactor design, separation-process engineering and a 24-EC laboratory thesis. UCR can construct strong molecular, medical and modelling pathways but lacks a continuous bioprocess-engineering sequence. The alternatives are defensible related biotechnology programmes, not engineering-degree equivalence."
    }
  ],
